# ============================================================================
# CHRISTIAN WIJAYA - Luxury Fashion
# .gitignore
#
# Rules here are deliberately EXPLICIT. This is a static HTML / CSS / vanilla
# JavaScript project with no build step, no package manager and no
# dependencies, so a broad ignore list would only risk hiding real project
# files. Nothing below may match anything the running website needs.
#
# REMEMBER: ignoring a file excludes it from Git only. Nothing here deletes
# or moves anything in the local working copy.
# ============================================================================


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. PRESERVED LOCAL ARCHIVES - kept on disk, never published
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The original first-generation site files.
backup_original/

# A snapshot taken immediately before the Phase 3 QA fixes. Retained locally as
# a rollback point; publishing it would show three apparent versions of the
# stylesheet with no way to tell which is authoritative.
backup_pre_phase3/

# The original HCI coursework document. It contains author identity metadata
# in its OOXML package (dc:creator / cp:lastModifiedBy) and an early mockup
# that predates the current build. It stays in the local project; it is not
# part of the published repository.
HCI.docx

# Empty placeholder created at project start.
HCI FIGMA.txt


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. FULL-RESOLUTION SOURCE IMAGES - kept locally, not published
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The website serves responsive derivatives from img/opt/ only. The originals
# in the img/ root are ~161 MB of editing source material that the running
# site never requests. Publishing them would grow the repository roughly
# thirteenfold for no functional gain.
#
# NOTE: img/opt/ is NOT ignored and must never be - the site loads from it.
img/*.jpg
img/*.jpeg
img/*.png
img/*.gif
img/*.webp
img/*.avif

# Source working folder for the catalogue photography. Not referenced by any
# page, script or stylesheet.
img/buat foto fashion/

# Six derivatives in img/opt/ that no product in the catalogue references.
# Excluded so the published image set is exactly the set the site serves.
img/opt/fashion luxury 1--240.jpg
img/opt/fashion luxury 1--612.jpg
img/opt/glassesshop-PFTjVsYUWzs-unsplash--1200.jpg
img/opt/glassesshop-PFTjVsYUWzs-unsplash--1920.jpg
img/opt/glassesshop-PFTjVsYUWzs-unsplash--240.jpg
img/opt/glassesshop-PFTjVsYUWzs-unsplash--700.jpg


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. DUPLICATE QA REPORT
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# documentation/QA_REPORT.md is the canonical copy referenced by README.md.
# This root-level duplicate is byte-identical and is kept locally only, so the
# published repository carries exactly one QA report.
#
# The leading slash is REQUIRED: without it this pattern would also match
# documentation/QA_REPORT.md, which must be published.
/QA_REPORT.md


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. LOCAL TOOLING AND TEST OUTPUT
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The behavioural and viewport QA suites were run from a scratch directory
# outside the repository so that they add no dependency weight to it.
scratch/
qa3.mjs
viewport.mjs
qa3_out.txt
vp_out.txt

# Local recordings and working artefacts from usability testing sessions.
documentation/usability/recordings/
documentation/usability/*.local.md


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. OPERATING SYSTEM ARTIFACTS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. EDITOR AND IDE ARTIFACTS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. LOGS AND TEMPORARY FILES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.cache/
.temp/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. SENSITIVE LOCAL FILES (defensive - none exist in this project today)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json
.netrc
.npmrc
id_rsa
id_ed25519


# ============================================================================
# NOT IGNORED ON PURPOSE
# ============================================================================
# README.md                        the repository front page
# index.html and the other 9 pages the site itself
# style.css, script.js, favicon.ico the whole application
# img/opt/                         every image the site actually loads
# screenshots/                     portfolio evidence, with MANIFEST.md
# documentation/QA_REPORT.md       the canonical QA report
# documentation/HCI_Report_Outline.md
# documentation/usability/         the usability testing instruments
# documentation/legacy/            the mockup extracted from HCI.docx
# tests/                           verify_selectors.py, _harness.html, _a11y.html
# ============================================================================
